[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/22","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/22/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/22/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/22/events","html_url":"https://github.com/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/pull/22","id":5923049336,"node_id":"PR_kwDOO-rWyc8AAAABJUUSGw","number":22,"title":"Stop propagating fork markers after a confirmed repair","user":{"login":"Abramov12","id":90068023,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwMDY4MDIz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90068023?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12","html_url":"https://github.com/Abramov12","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-19T11:32:26Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T11:32:26Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/pulls/22","html_url":"https://github.com/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/pull/22","diff_url":"https://github.com/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/pull/22.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/pull/22.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Clear stale fork markers along a confirmed repair's ancestry, so later canonical slots stop generating false fork reports. Keep discarded banks and sibling fork markers intact.\n\nFixes #21.\n\nAdded regression tests, including late parent metadata and GC of the dead bank's tombstone. Workspace tests, Clippy and formatting passed on Linux with Rust 1.95.0.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/22/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/22/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/21","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/21/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/21/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/21/events","html_url":"https://github.com/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/21","id":5879550504,"node_id":"I_kwDOO-rWyc8AAAABXnLSKA","number":21,"title":"A repaired dead slot makes every later slot fork-reported","user":{"login":"senzenn","id":185802908,"node_id":"U_kgDOCxMgnA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185802908?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn","html_url":"https://github.com/senzenn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-16T06:34:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T06:34:58Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"After the repair bank of a dead slot wins, each later slot gets ForksDetected while its parent is not rooted (forks.rs:598-602).\nOn Tower this does not stop, so every canonical slot gets a fork report and a WARN line.\n\nRepro on v0.12.0 (same on v0.11.0), all 68 slots from 43 to 110 get ForksDetected:\n```rust\nlet mut sm = BlocksStateMachine::default();\nseal_at(&mut sm, 41, 40, 410, CommitmentLevel::Confirmed);\nbuffer(&mut sm, 42, Some(41), 10, 2);\nsm.process_replay_event(dead(42).into()).unwrap();\nseal_at(&mut sm, 42, 41, 11, CommitmentLevel::Confirmed);\ndrain(&mut sm);\nlet mut forked = Vec::new();\nfor slot in 43u64..=110 {\n    seal_at(&mut sm, slot, slot - 1, slot * 10, CommitmentLevel::Confirmed);\n    if slot >= 74 {\n        let f = slot - 32;\n        let bank = if f == 42 { 11 } else { f * 10 };\n        sm.process_consensus_event(commitment(f, Some(f - 1), CommitmentLevel::Finalized, bank).into());\n    }\n    forked.extend(sorted_fork_reports(&drain(&mut sm)).into_iter().map(|(s, _)| s));\n}\nassert_eq!(forked, (43..=110).collect::<Vec<_>>());\n```\n\nExpected: no fork report for slots on the chain of the winning repair bank.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/21/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/21/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/20","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/20/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/20/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/20/events","html_url":"https://github.com/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/pull/20","id":5863110732,"node_id":"PR_kwDOO-rWyc8AAAABIlEbWw","number":20,"title":"Reject malformed stream input without panicking","user":{"login":"Abramov12","id":90068023,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwMDY4MDIz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90068023?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12","html_url":"https://github.com/Abramov12","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abramov12/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-15T08:53:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T08:54:53Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/pulls/20","html_url":"https://github.com/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/pull/20","diff_url":"https://github.com/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/pull/20.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/pull/20.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Drop malformed block and entry hashes instead of panicking. Reject block summaries whose slot conflicts with the buffered bank without consuming that bank.\r\n\r\nFixes #19.\r\n\r\nAdded regression tests. Workspace tests and Clippy passed on Linux with Rust 1.95.0. Formatting check passed.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/20/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/20/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/19","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/19/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/19/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/19/events","html_url":"https://github.com/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/19","id":5841961334,"node_id":"I_kwDOO-rWyc8AAAABXDVBdg","number":19,"title":"Bad stream input panics instead of being dropped","user":{"login":"senzenn","id":185802908,"node_id":"U_kgDOCxMgnA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185802908?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn","html_url":"https://github.com/senzenn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/senzenn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T04:30:44Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T04:32:55Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Version: 0.12.0 (b828807d)\n\nThese inputs panic in release builds. Other bad input already logs `UNEXPECTED` and is dropped, for example a duplicate BlockMeta (`wrapper.rs:427`).\n\n| Input | Panic | Line |\n|---|---|---|\n| BlockMeta `blockhash` that does not parse | `expect(\"blockhash format\")` | `dragonsmouth/proto_adapter.rs:47` |\n| Entry `hash` that is not 32 bytes | `expect(\"entry hash length\")` | `dragonsmouth/proto_adapter.rs:65` |\n| One `bank_id` in two slots | `assert_eq!(slot, frozen_block.slot)` | `state_machine.rs:1236` |\n\nThe third one happens because `block_buffer_map` is keyed by `bank_id` only, so the freeze gets the block of the other slot. On 0.12.0 the bank must also look complete, so it is rare. It can happen across a reconnect to another node, because client 15 bank IDs are per connection.\n\nshipstern tests hit the second and third on 0.11.0, which has the same code:\n- `proto_adapter.rs:65`: `entry hash length: TryFromSliceError(())`\n- `state_machine.rs:1213`: `assertion left == right failed, left: 101, right: 100`\n\nI did not run the first case.\n\nSuggested fix: `extract_geyser_ev_info` already returns `Option`, so return `None` for the first two. For the third, log `UNEXPECTED` and refuse the freeze. solana-rpc/shipstern#353 adds guards for all three, and shipstern would remove them.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/19/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpcpool/yellowstone-block-machine/issues/19/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}]